<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.1.4: Exploring a System of Equations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00376</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.1.4: Exploring a System of Equations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9b6f0ec2-d724-49f4-aafa-e0c9b6c681b7</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">At a fabric store, fabrics are sold by the yard. A dressmaker spent $36.35 on 4.25 yards
        of silk and cotton fabrics for a dress. Silk is $16.90 per yard, and cotton is $4 per yard.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Here is a system of equations that represents the constraints in the situation.</para>
      <para id="para-00003"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="true" fence="true" form="prefix">{</m:mo><m:mtable><m:mtr><m:mtd columnalign="left"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mspace width="2.2mm"/><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mspace width="2mm"/><m:mn>4.25</m:mn><m:mspace linebreak="newline"/><m:mn>16.90</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mi/><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>36.35</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mtd></m:mtr></m:mtable></m:mrow></m:mstyle></m:mrow></m:math></para><!--Q1-->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00004"> What does the solution to the system represent?</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00006">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The solution represents the combination
            of lengths of silk and cotton (in yards) that meet both constraints: they add up to 4.25
            yards, and the cost of buying both is $36.35.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q2-->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00007"> Find the solution to the system of equations.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00008">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00009">1.5 yards of silk and 2.75 yards of cotton.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
      <!--Q3-->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00010"> Explain or show how you know.</para>

        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00011">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00012">Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>The graphs of the equations intersect at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>2.75</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> 
              
                <media alt="Graph of a linear system. cotton (yards), silk (yards).">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_03_09_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              </item>
            <item>Solving by using a table gives <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1.5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2.75</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction
      End -->
    </section>
  </content>
